  "note": "Triennial election of the fifteen councillors of Londonderry Corporation, due Wednesday 17 May 1961: no contest. At the close of nominations on Wednesday 3 May six Nationalists were returned unopposed for the South Ward, six Unionists for the North Ward and three Unionists for the Waterside (Derry Journal, 5 May 1961). The Independent Labour Group decided not to contest. Names as in the Returning Officer's notice (surname and other names); the Derry Journal of 28 April 1961 names the six outgoing councillors as the Nationalist Party (Anti-Partition League, Derry branch) panel, Deeney as Seamus Deeney. Returned unopposed."
